        "id": 85389,
        "name": "Oaktree",
        "username": "Oaktree",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-24T20:49:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Does the same concept apply for villain cards that flip?&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For instance, if La Capitan flips at Start of Turn (according to the TIme Corsair side) does the Start of Turn text for her Split Across Time also apply this turn.&nbsp; Or is it that the SoT for the card was applied already and the flip side SoT is then not eligible for being applied that turn.</p><p>Also, I presume that Advanced Villain SoT text gets applied in order; e.g. you do regular SoT and if the card does not flip then Advanced text that is SoT is then read and activated.&nbsp; If the initial SoT text flipped the card the Advanced SoT is not gotten to and then does not apply?&nbsp; Or is it supposed to be taken as a large SoT block that applies before the flip?</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:03.476Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
